### Instruction:
Write a CSS style sheet to make all `<h2>` headings have a blue background, white text, and a border radius of 5 pixels. Additionally, ensure that the text is centered within the heading and that the background color changes to red when the heading is hovered over. Furthermore, add a transition effect of 0.5 seconds to smoothly animate the background color change. Finally, modify the CSS so that the border width is 2 pixels and the border color is green when the heading is active (clicked on).

### Response:
```css
h2 {
  background-color: blue;
  color: white;
  border-radius: 5px;
  text-align: center;
  padding: 10px;
  transition: background-color 0.5s;
}

h2:hover {
  background-color: red;
}

h2:active {
  border: 2px solid green;
}
```

### Instruction:
Create a CSS rule to apply a two-pixel red border to a text box when it is hovered over, and change the border color to blue when it is in focus. Additionally, include a smooth transition effect when the border color changes.

### Response:
```css
.textbox {
  border: 2px solid red;
  transition: border-color 0.5s ease;
}

.textbox:hover {
  border-color: red;
}

.textbox:focus {
  border-color: blue;
}
```

