### Instruction:
Edit the following HTML markup to add a "Welcome!" heading and ensure that the heading text is displayed in bold and colored red. Additionally, the section element should have a maximum width of 500 pixels, be aligned to the center of the page, and have a solid border of 2 pixels in green color.

### Response:
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
  section {
    max-width: 500px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    border: 2px solid green;
  }
  h1 {
    color: red;
    font-weight: bold;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
  <section>
    <h1>Welcome!</h1>
  </section>
</body>
</html>

### Instruction:
Write a CSS style to make a <div> element of width 500px and height 400px. Additionally, make the background color of the <div> element red and center align the text inside the <div>. The <div> element should also have a border of 1px solid black and a padding of 20px. The text inside the <div> element should have a font size of 20px and be bold.

### Response:
<style>
  .myDiv {
    width: 500px;
    height: 400px;
    background-color: red;
    text-align: center;
    border: 1px solid black;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .myDiv p {
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: bold;
  }
</style>

<div class="myDiv">
  <p>This is a sample text</p>
</div>

